nt":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Artificial Intelligence is\u00a0technology\u00a0that allows computers and machines to perform tasks that normally require human thinking, such as learning from data, recognizing patterns, understanding language, and making decisions.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-artificial-intelligence\/#faq-question-1785926705427","position":2,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-artificial-intelligence\/#faq-question-1785926705427","name":"2. What are the main types of AI?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"AI is\u00a0generally grouped\u00a0into Narrow AI, which handles specific tasks like voice assistants; General AI, a theoretical form that could match human intelligence across any task; and Super AI, a hypothetical stage where machines would exceed human intelligence entirely.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-artificial-intelligence\/#faq-question-1785926804109","position":3,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-artificial-intelligence\/#faq-question-1785926804109","name":"3. Is AI the same as machine learning?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Machine learning is a subset of AI. AI is the broader concept of machines mimicking human intelligence, while machine learning specifically refers to systems that learn from data rather than following fixed rules.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-artificial-intelligence\/#faq-question-1785926818056","position":4,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-artificial-intelligence\/#faq-question-1785926818056","name":"4. Will AI replace human jobs?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"AI will change many jobs rather than simply erasi